From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William Tambe <tambewilliam@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 11:49:17 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 5/8] tty: serial: Add the UART of the FonTamSOC

The UART, driven through hwdrvchar.h, a copy of the driver of the
FonTamSOC, transmits and receives 8N1 through buffers of 2048 bytes: its
receive interrupt drives the input, an hrtimer refills its transmit
buffer, as it has no transmit interrupt. The console and earlycon poll
it. A read with the receive buffer empty would stall the bus: only the
bytes which its usage counts are read.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: William Tambe <tambewilliam@gmail.com>
